1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:04,690
Hey, you guys? What are you doing tomorrow night?
嘿，你們明天晚上有事嗎？

2
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:08,100
Oh, well, let me see. I believe I'm..
嗯，讓我看看，我想我…

3
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:10,430
Yes, falling asleep in front of the TV.
是的，會在電視機前面睡著

4
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:14,840
Well, my agent hooked me up with six tickets to a great play.
我經紀人給我六張票 去看一出很棒的舞台劇

5
00:00:15,010 --> 00:00:16,640
I could fall asleep at a play.
我也可以在那出舞台劇演出時睡覺

6
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:19,840
- What is it? - It's a one-woman play called:
-是什麼樣的舞台劇？ -是一個女人的獨場戲叫做…

7
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:24,080
Why Don't You Like Me? A Bitter Woman's Journey Through Life.
《你為什麼不喜歡我？ 一個悲慘女人的生命歷程》

8
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:27,380
- That sounds interesting. - That does sound interesting.
-聽起來挺有趣的 -是聽起來挺有趣的

9
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:32,150
To listen to a woman complain for two hours. I don't think it gets bet..
聽一個女人抱怨兩個小時 我不認為那會更…

10
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:37,030
I know! I know. We can drive. We can vote. We can work.
我知道，我們可以開車 可以投票，可以工作

11
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,690
What more do these broads want?
那些女人還想要什麼呢？

12
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:43,030
Well, you guys will have a great time. I promise.
你們會喜歡的，我保證

13
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,930
What? How come you don't have to go?
什麼？為什麼你不去呢？

14
00:00:45,110 --> 00:00:46,700
I wish I could, but I found out..
我希望我可以，但是我發現…

15
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:50,370
that I have to be at work really early the next day, so I can't go.
我隔天要很早就起來工作 所以我不能去

16
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:53,140
But take the extra ticket and invite whoever you want.
但是你們可以用剩下的那張票 邀請任何人去都可以

17
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:56,280
Let's see. Who do I hate?
讓我瞧瞧我最恨誰呢？

18
00:00:58,490 --> 00:00:59,890
Oh, sorry.
對不起

19
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:01,650
- Oops, sorry. - Okay.
-哦，對不起 -好的

20
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:03,420
- Okay. - Okay. Up we go.
-好的 -好的，抬起來

21
00:01:03,590 --> 00:01:05,790
- Oh, gosh, okay! - All right.
-天啊，好的！ -好了

22
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,740
Can I ask you a question?
我可以問你一個問題嗎？

23
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:21,970
Do you think it's possible for two friends to fool around..
你覺得有沒有可能兩個朋友…

24
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:25,410
and not have it be a big deal?
打情罵俏後不會有事情發生？

25
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:29,310
No, I don't think that ever works. Why?
不可能，為什麼？

26
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,790
- No reason. - No, no. Rachel?
-沒事 -等一等，瑞秋？

27
00:01:33,090 --> 00:01:36,750
- Who do you want to fool around with? - Nobody! Forget it.
-你想要跟誰打情罵俏呢？ -沒有人！別想太多

28
00:01:37,030 --> 00:01:38,320
Joey?
喬伊嗎？

29
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:40,690
Maybe.
或許吧

30
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:43,250
- You can't. - Why?
-不行 -為什麼？

31
00:01:43,430 --> 00:01:44,960
Because!
因為！

32
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:50,830
Okay, seriously, did not understand a word you just said.
說真的，你說什麼 我一點都不瞭解

33
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:54,870
- In the hall. - Okay.
-到外面去 -好

34
00:01:57,550 --> 00:01:59,450
- You wanna fool around with Joey? - Yeah.
-你想要跟喬伊打情罵俏？ -是啊

35
00:01:59,610 --> 00:02:03,140
Ever since I had that dream about him, I can't get it out of my head.
自從我做過那個夢之後 我就一直忘不了

36
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:05,950
I mean, what's the big deal? People do it all the time.
我是說那又會怎樣？ 很多人都是那樣做的

37
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:08,780
Who do you know that are friends that just fool around?
你認識誰只在打情罵俏的？

38
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:13,190
Okay. Off the top of my head.. Don and Janet.
好的，隨便想想… 唐跟珍娜

39
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:16,090
- Who are they? - I know them from work.
-他們是誰？ -工作上認識的人

40
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:19,000
- Both of them? - No, just one of them.
-兩個都是嗎？ -不，只有其中一個

41
00:02:19,170 --> 00:02:20,960
Which one?
哪一個？

42
00:02:21,370 --> 00:02:24,070
I don't know. What were the names I just said?
我不知道，我剛才說了哪些名字呢？

43
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:27,000
No, Rachel, things could get incredibly complicated.
瑞秋，事情會變得很複雜的

44
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:30,630
All right. You're right. I won't do anything with Joey. I just thought it..
好吧，你說的對，我不會對喬伊怎樣的 我只是以為…

45
00:02:30,810 --> 00:02:35,680
Okay, so that's two cups of tarragon, one pound of baking soda and a red onion?
好的，那就兩杯的龍蒿、一磅的蘇打粉 還有紅洋蔥

46
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:38,850
What the hell are you cooking?
你是想要煮什麼呢？

47
00:02:40,627 --> 00:02:42,618
The One With The Soap Opera Party

00:02:43,627 --> 00:02:44,618
rainystar壓制iPod-MP4

48
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:34,540
You guys won't believe what I have to do for work today.
你們不會相信 我今天要做什麼樣的工作

49
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:39,270
Yes, but, Ross, you chose a career of talking about dinosaurs.
但是羅斯，是你自己選擇 要談論恐龍的工作的

50
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:43,840
There are these two professors who are joining my department..
有兩個教授要加入我的部門

51
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:48,010
and I have to meet them here and show them around campus.
而我要在這裡跟他們碰面 然後帶他們到校園看看

52
00:03:48,190 --> 00:03:49,350
What's so bad about that?
那怎麼會糟糕呢？

53
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:52,220
I just know they'll be a couple of old windbags..
我只知道他們會是那種老蓋仙

54
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:55,950
wearing tweed jackets with suede elbow patches.
穿著在手肘的地方 縫上仿麂皮的花呢外套

55
00:03:56,970 --> 00:03:58,020
Ross?
羅斯？

56
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:00,900
What? These aren't suede.
怎樣？這些不是仿麂皮

57
00:04:04,510 --> 00:04:07,530
Excuse me. I'm looking for someone.
不好意思，我在找人

58
00:04:07,710 --> 00:04:10,740
You don't, by any chance, know a Ross Geller?
你認不認識 一個叫做羅斯蓋勒的？

59
00:04:10,910 --> 00:04:12,210
No.
不認識

60
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:18,810
Hi. Hi, I'm Ross Geller.
嗨，我是羅斯蓋勒

61
00:04:18,990 --> 00:04:21,720
Oh, hi. I'm Professor Wheeler.
嗨，我是魏勒教授

62
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:26,190
Oh, that's.. That's.. That's nice.
喔，這…這太好了

63
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:28,190
It's good to meet you.
很高興見到你

64
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:31,230
Thank you so much for taking the time to show me around.
謝謝你願意花時間幫我介紹環境

65
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:33,230
No, it's no big deal.
不，這一點也不麻煩的

66
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:37,170
If I weren't doing this, I'd just, you know, be at the gym working out.
如果我沒有這樣做，反正我也只是 在健身房健身而已

67
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:40,070
Is he gonna introduce us?
他會介紹我們嗎？

68
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:43,570
I think we're just blurry shapes to him now.
我想他現在跟本就看不到我們

69
00:04:44,510 --> 00:04:46,740
By the way, I really enjoyed your paper..
對了，我真的很喜歡你寫的…

70
00:04:46,910 --> 00:04:51,370
on the connection between geographic isolation and rapid mutagenesis.
地域隔絕與快速突變之關係的論文

71
00:04:51,850 --> 00:04:54,520
I wrote that in one night.
我一個晚上就寫完了

72
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:58,750
Twenty bucks says they're married within the month.
我賭二十塊錢 他們一個月內就會結婚

73
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:02,060
Well, we should probably get going.
那麼我們最好走吧

74
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:05,020
You know, we've got a lot of ground to cover.
我們有很多地方要去

75
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,900
Isn't another professor supposed to come with us?
不是有另外一位教授要加入我們嗎？

76
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:10,760
I don't think so.
我想應該沒有

77
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:13,770
I'm pretty sure. A Professor Spafford from Cornell?
我非常確定 是從康乃爾來的史伯夫教授

78
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:17,040
Well, he's obviously late, and the rule in my class is:
他可能是遲到了 而我上課的規矩就是：

79
00:05:17,210 --> 00:05:21,150
If you can't come on time, then don't come at all.
如果你不能準時到，那就乾脆不要到

80
00:05:21,350 --> 00:05:24,480
An option that many of my students use.
我很多學生 最後都選擇後者

81
00:05:25,390 --> 00:05:27,450
- Shall we? - We shouldn't wait for him?
-我們要走了嗎？ -我們不用等他嗎？

82
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:30,890
You know what, he's a big boy. I'm sure he'll find us, okay?
你知道嗎？他是個大男孩了 我確定他可以找到我們的，好嗎？

83
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:33,460
- Professor Geller? - Oh, damn it!
-蓋勒教授嗎？ -喔，媽的！

84
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:46,800
Hi, Joey, it's Jan Rogers. Can 't wait for your party tonight.
嗨，喬伊，我是珍羅傑 等不及要參加你今晚的派對了

85
00:05:46,970 --> 00:05:51,600
Listen, I forgot your address. Can you give me a call? Thanks. Bye.
我忘記你的地址了，可以回電給我嗎？ 謝謝，拜

86
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:54,884
-Hi. -Hi.
-嗨 -嗨

87
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:56,240
What's happening?
怎麼了？

88
00:05:57,320 --> 00:06:00,690
It's a real shame you can't make it to that one-woman show tonight.
真可惜你沒有辦法參加 今晚的女人獨角戲

89
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:03,920
I'd love to, but I gotta get up so early the next day.
我也想去，但是我隔天要好早起來

90
00:06:04,090 --> 00:06:07,790
- You know me, work comes first. - Oh, yeah, yeah.
-你知道我的，工作最重要 -是啊，是啊

91
00:06:08,930 --> 00:06:12,830
Hi, Joey, it's Jan Rogers. Can 't wait for your party tonight.
嗨，喬伊，我是珍羅傑 等不及參加你今晚的派對了

92
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,930
Stupid Jan Rogers!
珍羅傑，你還真蠢！

93
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:19,910
You are having a party tonight?
你今晚要開派對？

94
00:06:20,070 --> 00:06:21,670
- No. - Joey!
-沒有 -喬伊！

95
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:23,470
Yeah.
是的

96
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:26,810
I'm kind of having a thing for the Days of Our Lives people.
我幫《我們的日子》的人員 辦了一個聚會

97
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:28,350
And you weren't gonna tell us?
而你卻不告訴我們？

98
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:30,950
How did you think you were gonna get away with that?
你認為你可以逃得掉嗎？

99
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,950
I do it every year.
我每年都這樣做啊

100
00:06:34,590 --> 00:06:36,610
You do that every year?!
你每年都這樣做！

101
00:06:36,790 --> 00:06:38,920
I didn't have to tell you that!
我不需要告訴你的！

102
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:41,990
God, I'm stupider than Jan Rogers!
天啊，我比珍羅傑還愚蠢！

103
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,190
That's why you got us tickets to that play, to get rid of us!
所以你就給我們去看舞台劇的票 甩掉我們！

104
00:06:46,370 --> 00:06:47,460
Yeah.
是啊

105
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:51,070
Last year is that why you sent us to that Medieval Times restaurant?
去年你就送我們去那間中古世紀餐廳？

106
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,470
Yeah.
是啊

107
00:06:53,370 --> 00:06:57,940
And the year before that, you set up that nighttime tour of that button factory?
而前年你幫我們安排鈕扣工廠之旅？

108
00:06:58,110 --> 00:07:01,240
I can't believe you guys went for that one.
我不敢相信那個你們也會去

109
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,680
Why wouldn't you invite us to your parties?
你為什麼不邀請我們參加你的派對呢？

110
00:07:04,250 --> 00:07:08,150
You're fine, okay? But everyone else acts like an idiot around famous people.
你還好，但是其他人在名人面前 都表現的像傻瓜一樣

111
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:11,260
Well, then, so just invite me.
那麼，就只邀請我就好了啊

112
00:07:11,790 --> 00:07:15,020
Please, I was trying to be nice. You're the worst one.
拜託，我只是在說好聽話 你是最糟糕的

113
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:19,190
Joey, come on! Please, please? Let me come. I will behave. I promise.
喬伊，別這樣！拜託啦 讓我參加，我會克制自己，我保證

114
00:07:19,370 --> 00:07:22,860
- I will behave. Please, please, please. - Okay, fine. You can come.
-我會克制自己，拜託 -好啦，你可以參加

115
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:26,670
But don't tell anybody else. It's up on the roof at 8.
但是不要告訴其他人 八點鐘在屋頂上面

116
00:07:26,910 --> 00:07:28,430
A soap-opera roof party?!
肥皂劇屋頂派對！

117
00:07:28,610 --> 00:07:32,240
I'm going to a soap-opera roof party! Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
我要參加肥皂劇屋頂派對！ 喔，我的天啊！…

118
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:37,010
And it's out of my system.
好了，發洩完了

119
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:48,220
And then my wife and I went on a cruise to the Galapagos.
然後我老婆跟我搭游輪到加拉巴哥

120
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:52,630
There was a seafood buffet you wouldn't believe.
你們不會相信他們的 隨你吃海鮮餐廳有多棒

121
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:57,900
There were clams and mussels and oysters..
有蛤蜊、河蚌還有生蠔

122
00:07:58,070 --> 00:08:00,370
and cracked crab..
還有螃蟹…

123
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:02,700
and snow crab..
還有花蟹…

124
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:05,370
and king crab.
還有帝王蟹

125
00:08:05,550 --> 00:08:08,740
It's a pity I'm allergic to shellfish.
真可惜我對帶殼類海鮮對敏

126
00:08:10,250 --> 00:08:13,190
So where did you get your undergraduate degree?
你大學是在哪念的呢？

127
00:08:13,350 --> 00:08:17,090
- And that's not all I'm allergic to. - Oh, it's not over.
-而且我不只對那些過敏 -喔，還沒有結束啊

128
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:21,390
I'm also allergic to peanuts and cashews..
我還有對花生跟腰果過敏

129
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,790
and almonds and filberts..
還有杏仁果跟榛果…

130
00:08:23,970 --> 00:08:25,560
So basically all nuts!
所以基本上是所有的堅果類！

131
00:08:25,870 --> 00:08:28,030
Interestingly, no.
有趣的是，並不盡然

132
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:32,670
You're kind of playing it fast and loose with the word "interesting."
你在說「有趣的是」時說的挺慢的 讓人以為就是如此

133
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:37,000
If you'll excuse me, I'm going to use the restroom.
不好意思失陪一下，我要去洗手間

134
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:39,200
When I come back, remind me to tell you..
當我回來的時候，提醒我告訴你們…

135
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:44,150
about the different types of animal dander I'm allergic to.
我對哪些動物過敏

136
00:08:46,050 --> 00:08:48,320
Oh, my God!
喔，我的天啊！

137
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:50,680
I've lost the will to live.
我已經喪失活下去的意志力了

138
00:08:52,390 --> 00:08:53,880
- Let's ditch him. - What?
-我們甩了他 -什麼？

139
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:56,760
While he's still in the bathroom. I am begging you.
在他還在洗手間的時候，我求求你

140
00:08:56,930 --> 00:09:00,730
Okay. Okay, fine, but I just have one question for you.
好的，但是我有個問題要先問你

141
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:03,960
When we exit, should we walk or run..
我們出去的時候 應該是用走的、跑的…

142
00:09:04,170 --> 00:09:06,440
or prance or stroll..?
跳的還是散步出去？

143
00:09:06,610 --> 00:09:10,040
Stop it! Stop it! He talks slow, but he might pee fast. Okay, let's move!
別說了！他的話說得慢 搞不好尿得快，我們快走！

144
00:09:19,050 --> 00:09:23,850
- We actually managed to salvage the day. - Yeah, we did.
-幸好今天過的還不錯 -是的，沒錯

145
00:09:24,030 --> 00:09:26,430
Thanks for spending so much time with me.
謝謝你花這麼多時間陪我

146
00:09:26,590 --> 00:09:29,890
I'm so lucky it worked out you don't have class on Tuesday.
我很幸運，你星期二沒有課

147
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:31,290
Right.
沒錯

148
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:38,400
Oh, hey, you guys, this is Charlie.
你們好，這位是查莉

149
00:09:38,610 --> 00:09:41,440
Charlie, this is Phoebe and my sister, Monica.
查莉，這是菲比，還有我妹妹摩妮卡

150
00:09:41,610 --> 00:09:44,770
- Hi. - Charlie will be joining my department.
-嗨 -查莉將要加入我們繫上

151
00:09:44,950 --> 00:09:47,140
- You're a paleontologist too? - Yeah.
-你也是古生物學家嗎？ -是的

152
00:09:47,450 --> 00:09:49,470
Oh, okay. Now, what do you think..
那好，你對於…

153
00:09:49,650 --> 00:09:53,980
of Renyard's new theory of species variegation in segmented arthropods?
雷諾的分割類人猿物種多樣性的新理論 有何評價？

154
00:09:55,860 --> 00:10:00,620
Well, I think he's a little out there, but he does have some interesting ideas.
我覺得他有點太前衛了 但是他是有些有趣的觀點

155
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:04,260
Oh, I'm sorry. I have to take this. Excuse me.
很抱歉，我要接一下電話 不好意思

156
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:07,130
Renyard's theory of species variegation?
雷諾的物種多樣性？

157
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:11,400
I saw the article on your coffee table. I memorized the title to freak you out.
我在你的咖啡桌上看到一篇文章 我背下了標題想要來嚇你

158
00:10:14,610 --> 00:10:16,270
So did you two have fun?
你們倆個相處的愉快嗎？

159
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:18,940
Oh, my God. She's great.
天啊，她真的是太棒了

160
00:10:19,110 --> 00:10:23,410
We have so much in common, and she's just cool, you know? And funny.
我們有許多共同點，她真是太酷了 你知道嗎？還很風趣

161
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:27,210
And I don't know if you've noticed, but she's a hottie!
而且我不知道你有沒有注意到 但是她真辣！

162
00:10:27,590 --> 00:10:28,950
Hi!
嗨！

163
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:38,560
Hi, you guys. Listen, you know what, I'm not feeling really well..
嗨，大家聽著 我覺得不太舒服…

164
00:10:38,730 --> 00:10:42,170
and I don't think I'm gonna get to go to the play.
我想我可能不能去看舞台劇表演了

165
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:43,670
Really? What's wrong?
真的嗎？怎麼了？

166
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:46,030
I don't know. I think it's kind of serious.
我不知道，好像蠻嚴重的

167
00:10:46,210 --> 00:10:49,670
You know, I was watching this thing on TV this morning..
我今天早上在電視上有看到…

168
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:54,080
about Newcastle disease, and I think I might have it.
什麼關於新堡疾病的 我想我可能感染到了

169
00:10:54,450 --> 00:10:56,940
Newcastle disease is a secretion-borne virus..
新堡疾病是跟分泌物有關的病毒

170
00:10:57,150 --> 00:10:59,880
that only affects chickens and other poultry.
只有雞或是其它家禽才會被傳染到

171
00:11:02,060 --> 00:11:03,820
Okay, who's this?
好的，這是誰呢？

172
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:07,690
I'm sorry. Rachel, this is Charlie Wheeler. She's a colleague.
抱歉，瑞秋，這位是查莉魏勒 她是我同事

173
00:11:07,860 --> 00:11:09,760
Hi. Well, I would shake your hand..
嗨，我應該要跟你握手的…

174
00:11:09,930 --> 00:11:13,230
but I'm sure you don't want to get my chicken disease.
但是我想你不會想要 被傳染到我的雞病

175
00:11:13,770 --> 00:11:16,970
- Rachel, can I see you for a second? - Sure.
-瑞秋，我可以跟你談一下嗎？ -當然

176
00:11:22,210 --> 00:11:23,440
You're not sick.
你沒有生病

177
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:25,580
What? Yes, I am!
什麼？我當然有！

178
00:11:25,750 --> 00:11:28,180
Okay, then why are you all dressed up?
那麼為什麼你要穿成這樣呢？

179
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:34,220
When you're sick, you do whatever you can to make yourself feel better.
當你生病的時候，你會做任何事情 來讓自己覺得好過一些

180
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:39,160
You just want to stay home so you can make a move on Joey.
你只是想要待在家裡 對喬伊採取行動

181
00:11:39,330 --> 00:11:42,060
No, I heard you before. That is so not what this is.
不是，我聽進去了你之前說的話 事情不是這樣的

182
00:11:42,230 --> 00:11:44,200
Okay, then what is this?
好的，那是怎麼回事呢？

183
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,600
Okay.
好的

184
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:50,460
Joey is having a secret Days of Our Lives party up on the roof.
喬伊幫《我們的日子》在屋頂舉行 秘密派對

185
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:53,160
And he sent you guys to the play to get rid of you.
他送你們去看舞台劇來甩掉你們

186
00:11:53,610 --> 00:11:55,340
What?!
什麼？

187
00:11:56,140 --> 00:11:57,410
What? What's going on?
什麼？這是怎麼回事？

188
00:11:57,580 --> 00:12:01,210
Joey is having a secret Days of Our Lives party up on the roof!
喬伊幫《我們的日子》 在屋頂舉行秘密派對

189
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:05,820
He didn't want you to know about it, but I came over here to tell you.
他不想要讓你們知道 但是我還是過來告訴你們了

190
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:09,910
- You came to say you were sick. - All right, professor or detective?
-你是過來說你生病的 -你到底是教授還是偵探？

191
00:12:11,030 --> 00:12:14,650
Wait, Joey's having a party, and he wasn't gonna invite us?
等等，喬伊要開派對 但不邀請我們？

192
00:12:14,830 --> 00:12:18,420
He does it every year. That's why he's sending you to the play.
他每年都那樣做的 這就是為什麼他要請我們去看舞台劇

193
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:22,760
That's why he sent us to that medieval restaurant and to that button factory.
這就是為什麼他請我們去中古世紀餐廳 還有鈕扣工廠

194
00:12:22,940 --> 00:12:25,240
And that horrible museum tour?
而有那次糟糕的博物館之旅嗎？

195
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:27,370
No, I arranged that.
不是，那是我安排的

196
00:12:30,950 --> 00:12:34,140
Hey, you guys, I'm turning in. Have fun.
你們好，我過來打招呼 祝你們玩的愉快

197
00:12:37,550 --> 00:12:39,250
We know about your party, Joey.
我們知道你的派對了，喬伊

198
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:42,950
- What party? - The game's over. Take off your robe.
-什麼派對？ -遊戲結束了，把睡袍脫掉吧

199
00:12:44,130 --> 00:12:45,890
Okay, I mean..
好的，我是說…

200
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:51,300
Close it up! Close it up!
穿起來！穿起來！

201
00:12:53,830 --> 00:12:55,130
Nice to meet you.
很高興見到你

202
00:13:03,610 --> 00:13:05,550
Hey, you made it! All right!
嘿，你來了！太好了！

203
00:13:05,710 --> 00:13:07,910
Glad you could make it. Thanks for coming.
很高興你來了，謝謝你參加

204
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:11,250
- Oh, my God. Kyle Lowder! - Hi.
-我的天啊，凱爾羅德！ -嗨

205
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:13,650
I love you!
我愛你！

206
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:17,480
Hey. That's why I didn't invite you. You have to calm down, all right?
喂，這就是我為什麼不想邀請你 你要冷靜點，好嗎？

207
00:13:17,690 --> 00:13:19,660
Just go get yourself a drink or something.
去喝點飲料什麼的

208
00:13:19,830 --> 00:13:22,730
Oh, yeah, that's what you want. My inhibitions lowered.
是啊，你就是要讓我的自制力潰堤

209
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:26,560
Oh, my God, can you believe we're surrounded by all this?
我的天啊，你敢相信我們 被這些人包圍著嗎？

210
00:13:26,730 --> 00:13:28,260
I can barely control myself.
我幾乎控制不了自己

211
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:31,060
Monica, you might want to remember that you're married.
摩妮卡，你該瞭解到你已經結婚了

212
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:33,470
Where is Chandler anyway?
錢德呢？

213
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,170
Oh, my God! Chandler!
我的天啊！錢德！

214
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:44,580
Where the hell is everybody?
大家死哪去了？

215
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:49,420
Why Don't You Like Me?
你為什麼不喜歡我？

216
00:13:53,330 --> 00:13:56,630
Chapter 1: My First Period.
第一章：我的第一次生理期

217
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:03,290
Hey, Joey said no autographs.
喬伊說不能要簽名的

218
00:14:03,470 --> 00:14:05,600
But if she's getting one, I want one too!
但是如果她有，那我也要！

219
00:14:05,770 --> 00:14:09,830
"To Monica." And none of this "best wishes" crap. I want "love."
「給摩妮卡」，而且別寫什麼 「祝福」之類的，要寫「愛」

220
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:15,050
Okay, actually, Mon, Matthew was giving me his phone number.
事實上，摩妮卡 馬修只是給我他的電話

221
00:14:15,220 --> 00:14:18,050
Oh, man! If I had known I was coming to this party..
天啊！如果我知道 我要參加這個派對…

222
00:14:18,250 --> 00:14:20,120
I never would've gotten married!
我就一定不會結婚！

223
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:23,250
- It was nice to meet you. - Nice to meet you.
-很高興認識你 -很高興認識你

224
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:25,620
- Call me. - We will!
-打電話給我 -我們會的！

225
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:31,920
Look at you with all the guys! I guess you've forgotten all about Joey.
瞧瞧你周旋在眾多男生之間！ 我猜你把喬伊都忘光了

226
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:34,860
Yeah, well, I guess I have forgotten about Joey.
是的，我想我是忘了喬伊

227
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:37,440
And clearly, you've forgotten about Chandler.
而很明顯地，你也忘了錢德

228
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:40,530
Please. Chandler's the love of my life.
拜託，錢德是我的摯愛

229
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:42,800
Oh, leather pants! Have mercy!
皮褲耶！不會吧！

230
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:49,270
So do you get to go to things like this often?
你常常參加這種派對嗎？

231
00:14:49,450 --> 00:14:51,510
Come on, this is New York.
是啊，這裡是紐約耶

232
00:14:51,690 --> 00:14:55,210
I mean, one night you're at a rooftop party filled with soap stars..
我是說，有時候晚上在屋頂上 跟很多肥皂劇明星開派對…

233
00:14:55,390 --> 00:14:57,580
and the next night, you're..
有時候，就是…

234
00:14:58,190 --> 00:15:00,460
Who am I kidding, this is so cool.
我是在騙誰呢，這實在太酷了！

235
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:05,320
So it's probably gonna be hard for you to leave Boston, huh?
離開波士頓對你而言 一定很困難吧？

236
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:09,370
Actually, I'm kind of happy to be leaving. I just broke up with someone.
事實上我很高興離開那 我剛剛分手

237
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,800
Oh, so sad.
真令人傷心

238
00:15:12,340 --> 00:15:15,040
Still, it can't be easy for you to leave Harvard.
但是離開哈佛 一定也是不容易

239
00:15:15,210 --> 00:15:19,270
Especially after working with a Nobel Prize winner like Albert Wintermeyer.
尤其是跟諾貝爾得主 亞伯特溫麥爾共事過

240
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:22,510
Actually, Albie is the guy I broke up with.
事實上，阿亞就是我分手的人

241
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:25,780
- You dated Albert Wintermeyer? - Yeah.
-你跟亞伯特溫麥爾交往過？ -是的

242
00:15:25,950 --> 00:15:28,890
And you called him "Albie"?
而你叫他「阿亞」？

243
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:33,920
I mean, that's like calling Albert Einstein..
我是說，這就像是叫 亞伯特愛因斯坦…

244
00:15:34,730 --> 00:15:36,130
Albie.
阿亞一樣

245
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:39,790
Yeah, well, he is a brilliant man.
對，他是個很聰明的男人

246
00:15:39,970 --> 00:15:42,130
You think? I mean, you dated the guy..
你認為嗎？我是說，你跟一個…

247
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:45,640
who improved the accuracy of radiocarbon dating by a factor of 10!
提升了碳十四的精準測定法的 男人交往！

248
00:15:45,810 --> 00:15:50,270
Yes, and while that is everything one looks for in a boyfriend..
是的，而那正是每個人 對男朋友的需求

249
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,110
he had a lot of issues.
他有很多問題

250
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:54,140
Oh, like what?
像是什麼呢？

251
00:15:54,550 --> 00:15:57,710
I'm sorry. I don't mean to pry. It's just that this must be..
很抱歉，我不是要刺探隱私 只是跟…

252
00:15:57,890 --> 00:16:02,020
what regular people experience when they watch Access Hollywood.
一般人看《娛樂新聞》 有一樣的反應

253
00:16:02,490 --> 00:16:04,250
Okay, you want the dirt?
好的，你想要知道內幕嗎？

254
00:16:04,430 --> 00:16:06,550
Albie was seriously insecure.
阿亞有很嚴重的沒安全感

255
00:16:06,730 --> 00:16:09,920
He was really intimidated by the guy I dated before him.
他對我之前男朋友感到非常地不安

256
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:13,500
Who's intimidating to a guy who won the Nobel Prize?
誰能夠威脅到諾貝爾獎得主呢？

257
00:16:13,670 --> 00:16:15,660
A guy who won two.
得過兩次諾貝爾獎的人

258
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:17,500
Two? What..?
兩次？什麼？

259
00:16:17,670 --> 00:16:20,640
Don't tell me you dated Benjamin Hobart?
別告訴我你跟班傑明赫伯交往過？

260
00:16:20,810 --> 00:16:22,710
Yeah, for three years.
是的，交往了三年

261
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:24,280
Oh, my God.
我的天啊

262
00:16:25,110 --> 00:16:29,450
Have you ever been in a relationship with someone who hasn't won the Nobel Prize?
你有沒有跟沒得過 諾貝爾獎的人交往過呢？

263
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:32,510
No.
沒有

264
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:35,450
But there was my first boyfriend, Billy.
但我的第一個男朋友比利沒有

265
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:37,950
Oh, yeah? No Nobel Prizes for him?
是嗎？他沒有得諾貝爾嗎？

266
00:16:38,130 --> 00:16:41,390
No, but he did just win the MacArthur "genius grant."
沒有，但是他倒是得過麥克阿瑟的 「天才獎學金」

267
00:16:42,330 --> 00:16:44,420
What a loser.
真是個窩囊廢

268
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,900
Some more wine?
要再喝點酒嗎？

269
00:16:52,070 --> 00:16:54,510
Hey, Ross. How's it going with Charlie?
羅斯，跟查莉進行的如何呢？

270
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,540
Oh, great. After I finish my wine..
很好，在我喝完酒之後…

271
00:16:56,710 --> 00:17:00,650
I'm gonna blow my average-sized brains out.
我正常的腦袋會爆炸

272
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:02,380
What's the matter?
怎麼了？

273
00:17:02,550 --> 00:17:07,180
She only dates geniuses and Nobel Prize winners.
她只跟天才還有諾貝爾獎得主交往

274
00:17:07,350 --> 00:17:10,150
Oh, my God, at the Chinese restaurant earlier today..
我的天啊，今天稍早在中國餐廳…

275
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:14,660
I put chopsticks in my mouth and pretended to be a woolly mammoth.
我把筷子放在嘴中假裝是長毛象

276
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:17,060
I always loved that.
我很喜歡那樣耶

277
00:17:17,230 --> 00:17:20,720
Of course you would! Your brains are smaller than mine!
當然你會喜歡，你的大腦比我的小！

278
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:24,900
I can't compete with the guys she goes out with.
我不能跟她交往過的男人相比

279
00:17:25,070 --> 00:17:27,600
They're so out of my league.
他們比我好太多了

280
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:29,240
Oh, my God!
我的天啊！

281
00:17:29,410 --> 00:17:31,380
- Worse? - Oh, much, much worse.
-還有更糟的嗎？ -比那還糟

282
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:35,610
I did my impression of Joan Rivers as one of the earliest amphibians.
我還模仿瓊瑞薇演出最早的兩棲人

283
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:37,010
"Can we walk?"
「我們可以去散步嗎？」

284
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:41,520
- Oh, you like that? - No.
-你喜歡嗎？ -不

285
00:17:41,690 --> 00:17:42,920
What?
怎樣？

286
00:17:43,090 --> 00:17:46,420
Come on! I think that's funny!
別這樣！我覺得這樣很好笑啊！

287
00:17:47,090 --> 00:17:48,720
Woolly mammoth.
長毛象

288
00:17:48,900 --> 00:17:50,590
It's good!
很好笑耶！

289
00:17:52,730 --> 00:17:56,860
I bet you're thinking that now would be a great time for an intermission, huh?
我想你們一定在想現在該中場休息了 是嗎？

290
00:17:57,040 --> 00:17:59,700
Oh, yes. God, yes.
是的，上帝，拜託

291
00:18:00,270 --> 00:18:02,210
Well, you're not gonna get one!
你們不會休息的！

292
00:18:02,380 --> 00:18:05,740
Because in life, there are no intermissions, people!
因為現實生活是沒有中場休息的！

293
00:18:07,050 --> 00:18:10,810
Now, Chapter 7: Divorce is a Four-Letter Word!
現在開始第七章：離婚是四個字母！

294
00:18:12,650 --> 00:18:15,140
How could he leave me?!
他怎麼可以離開我呢？

295
00:18:16,890 --> 00:18:19,550
I don't know. You seem lovely.
我不知道，你看起來挺可愛的

296
00:18:26,530 --> 00:18:30,770
Ross, this is one of my costars, Dirk. Dirk, this is my good friend Ross.
羅斯，這是我同事登克 登克，這是我好朋友羅斯

297
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:33,340
- Nice to meet you. - So, what show are you on?
-很高興認識你 -你是哪出戲的呢？

298
00:18:33,510 --> 00:18:36,910
I'm not an actor. I'm a professor of paleontology.
我不是演員，我是古生物學教授

299
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:39,470
That's science.
科學的東東

300
00:18:40,050 --> 00:18:42,780
Hey, well, listen, I play a scientist on Days.
嘿，聽著，我在 《我們的日子》裡面演的是科學家

301
00:18:42,950 --> 00:18:45,820
Yeah, my character just won a Nobel Prize.
我的角色剛剛贏得諾貝爾獎

302
00:18:47,750 --> 00:18:52,620
Ross, Dirk was wondering about the woman you brought and if you guys are together?
羅斯，登克想問你帶來的那個女生 是不是你的女朋友

303
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:55,090
Well, no, but..
